* ''Two house readings under the clock law'' (controller, 2026-11-07, under the 2026-11-06 delegation). The clock census reads `// PACING: <reason>` beside a clock that decides nothing (a poll cadence or debounce whose end an event or a named `LIVENESS` bound decides), the way it reads `// LIVENESS: <reason>`; a marker without its reason counts as unmarked. A teardown drain runs in two phases with no island clock: the island submits every owed write and sends `receipt:asks-done`; the vessel answers as asked and sends `receipt:close`; the port closing or the worker exiting ends receipts the same way, an owed title reporting unsaved by name (`L29`).

